     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ASHAs protest in Karnataka demanding ₹15,000 monthly pay</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Accredited Social Health Activists (ASHAs) staged a protest in Ballari on Thursday as part of a state-wide 'Protest Week.' Organized by the Karnataka State United ASHA Workers’ Association, workers demanded that Central and State government incentives and honorariums be consolidated into a fixed monthly payment of ₹15,000.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/ashas-protest-in-karnataka-demanding-15000-monthly-pay.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Demonstrators highlighted stagnant pay, noting only a ₹1,500 increase over nine years, alongside delayed payments and technical issues with mandatory mobile applications. Protesters submitted a memorandum to the Chief Minister and Health Minister, seeking immediate release of pending funds and the cessation of forced tasks outside National Health Mission guidelines.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Strong reportage that captures the core demands and context of the protest without unnecessary filler.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/ashas-stage-protest-seeking-15000-monthly-remuneration/article71559524.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
