     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>CPI(M) Protests Over Pending Land Documents in Mulagada</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The CPI(M) Visakhapatnam district secretary M. Jaggu Naidu led a protest at the Mulagada MRO office, demanding the issuance of registration documents and conveyance deeds for local property owners. Approximately 10,000 residents in wards 75 to 82, including areas like Malkapuram, Jai Andhra Colony, and Gullalapalem, remain in possession of pattas but lack formal property registration.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/cpim-protests-over-pending-land-documents-in-mulagada.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Protesters submitted a memorandum and collective applications to the Mulagada tahsildar to address these long-standing administrative delays. The party is pressing for immediate action to provide the necessary legal documentation to these house owners, who currently face uncertainty regarding their property status despite having been issued pattas.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the protest and the specific grievances of the Mulagada residents.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/cpim-seeks-registration-documents-for-mulagada-residents/article71560580.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
