  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/national">national</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-08 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Gaurav Gogoi Demands Answers on Missing Woman Pushed to Bangladesh</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Assam Congress president Gaurav Gogoi has demanded that Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma disclose the whereabouts of Mumtaz Begum, a Nagaon woman allegedly pushed across the India-Bangladesh border in mid-June. The woman's son, Momruz Ali, has disputed the Chief Minister’s claim that he remains in daily contact with his mother, stating he has had no communication with her since her disappearance.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/gaurav-gogoi-demands-answers-on-missing-woman-pushed-to-bang.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gogoi previously wrote to External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar, noting the Gauhati High Court had ordered a fresh review of the woman's case before she was taken into custody. He insists that authorities must locate and reunite the family immediately.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief clearly outlines the conflict regarding the missing woman and the specific assertions made by Gaurav Gogoi.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/mumtaz-begum-whereabouts-gaurav-gogoi-questions-himanta-sarma-over-assam-pushback-ptag-3012846-2026-10-08?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-08/gaurav-gogoi-demands-answers-on-missing-woman-pushed-to-bang" data-title="Gaurav Gogoi Demands Answers on Missing Woman Pushed to Bangladesh"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
