     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-08 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>GTA VI Leaks Continue with Extensive Nude Gameplay Video</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#GTA VI</span> <span>#Leaks</span> <span>#Gaming</span> <span>#Cybersecurity</span></div>
       <p>New leaks surrounding Grand Theft Auto VI have emerged, featuring a 25-minute gameplay video that has surfaced online. As reported by Kotaku, this footage displays the character Jason running completely naked through various parts of Vice City for almost the entire duration. Specific scenes show Jason unclothed while on a motorbike, at a beach-side coffee store, and during conversations with other characters. Additionally, a clip at the end of the video briefly reveals Lucia mostly naked, shown from behind.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/gta-vi-leaks-continue-with-extensive-nude-gameplay-video.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The latest leak is attributed to Cyberleek, a known GTA leaker. Cyberleek had reportedly cashed out on a memecoin and seemingly disappeared earlier this year, but has now returned to distribute this extensive new video. According to Kotaku, the footage includes light story spoilers, commencing with a cutscene featuring Jason and Lucia that transitions into a dirt bike race, indicating one of the game's scripted missions. Cyberleek further demonstrates first-person driving footage from Jason, followed by a street race, and is also noted for &quot;seemingly conjuring a tank out of the air,&quot; alongside advertising a crypto coin within the video.</p><p>This incident follows a history of leaks that have prompted strong reactions from the game's creators. Cyberleek had previously shared a slew of other GTA VI clips in the period leading up to the game's official &quot;extended look&quot; on Netflix. Rockstar Games publicly described these earlier leaks as &quot;heartbreaking,&quot; and Take-Two has since requested multiple subpoenas in its efforts to identify the &quot;alleged infringers&quot; responsible for releasing game footage. These actions come after a massive collection of videos leaked in 2022, a breach that ultimately led to the hacker being sentenced to life in hospital prison. Grand Theft Auto VI is currently available for preorder and is slated for release on November 19th.</p><p>What to watch: Further legal and enforcement actions by Rockstar Games and Take-Two against those leaking game content.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the report from The Verge, covering the contents of the leaked video, the identity of the leaker, and the broader context of the company's legal battles.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1007770/gta-6-leaks-cyberleek-jason-lucia-naked" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
