     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Haryana launches drive to clear pending electoral roll notices</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Haryana Chief Electoral Officer’s office has launched a three-day drive to resolve pending notices issued during the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls. Camps and house-to-house collections are occurring through October 9 at polling stations to address discrepancies among 4,491,923 total notices generated across the state.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/haryana-launches-drive-to-clear-pending-electoral-roll-notic.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>On October 7 and 8, officials successfully disposed of 57,339 pending hearing cases, leaving 285,834 cases remaining. The state aims to finalize all hearings by October 28 to ensure the final electoral roll is published on November 6, despite challenges cited by Booth-Level Officers regarding heavy workloads and administrative time constraints.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is highly dense, accurately reflecting all the statistics and administrative challenges cited in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/haryana/haryana-ceo-launches-three-day-drive-to-clear-pending-sir-notices/article71560408.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
