     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-08 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>INDIA Bloc Leaders Stage Rajghat Satyagraha Against CEC</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>For the third consecutive day, leaders of the INDIA bloc staged a peaceful satyagraha at Mahatma Gandhi’s memorial at Rajghat to protest against alleged vote theft and demand the removal of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge stated the leaders prayed for the government to gain the wisdom to protect voting rights and remove the CEC.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/india-bloc-leaders-stage-rajghat-satyagraha-against-cec.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The opposition alliance, including representatives from the Samajwadi Party, Shiv Sena (UBT), and NCP (SP), plans to march toward Rashtrapati Bhavan on October 9. Rahul Gandhi accused Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Union Home Minister Amit Shah of hijacking the country and undermining the Constitution.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief covers the essential points of the protest, the participants, and the stated demands of the INDIA bloc.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/opposition-leaders-pray-at-rajghat-for-government-to-get-wisdom-to-remove-cec-say-protest-will-continue/article71560872.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-08/india-bloc-leaders-stage-rajghat-satyagraha-against-cec" data-title="INDIA Bloc Leaders Stage Rajghat Satyagraha Against CEC"><b>Share:</b>
