     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-10-08 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Nears TB Elimination Goal Amidst Declining Incidence</h1>
       
       <p>India is reportedly close to achieving its goal of eliminating tuberculosis, with Union Minister Nadda highlighting significant progress. The nation has seen its TB incidence decline by 21 per cent, a figure that markedly surpasses the global decline rate of 12 per cent.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/india-nears-tb-elimination-goal-amidst-declining-incidence.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Furthermore, treatment coverage for tuberculosis in India has reached an impressive 92 per cent. This national achievement compares favorably to the global treatment coverage, which currently stands at 78 per cent.</p><p>Nadda emphasized the critical need for a &quot;last push&quot; to fully realize the &quot;TB-free India&quot; objective. These sustained efforts reflect a concerted drive towards eradicating the disease nationwide, building on the substantial progress already made.</p><p>What to watch: Continued national efforts for the final push towards TB elimination.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article captures the core statistics and the minister's call to action from the summary accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/policy/india-very-close-to-achieving-goal-of-eliminating-tuberculosis-nadda/134790049" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
