     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-08 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Rejects Musk's Starlink Discrimination Claim Amid Regulatory Hurdles</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Technology</span> <span>#Satellite Internet</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>India has rejected Elon Musk’s assertion that Starlink, SpaceX’s satellite internet service, faces unfair blocking from launching in the country. This pushback comes as SpaceX continues to navigate regulatory processes and partnerships with major Indian telecom operators in its effort to launch commercial services in one of the world's largest internet markets, as reported by TechCrunch.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/india-rejects-musks-starlink-discrimination-claim-amid-regul.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>On Wednesday, Musk accused unnamed &quot;oligarchs&quot; of hindering Starlink's launch to maintain a &quot;monopolistic chokehold&quot; on India, characterizing it as a &quot;crime against the people of India.&quot; He argued that Starlink could provide affordable, high-speed internet to underserved populations. Hours later, India's Ministry of Communications countered, stating its regulatory framework for satellite communications is &quot;fair and non-discriminatory.&quot; The ministry's statement confirmed that Starlink and two other licensed satellite operators are at &quot;broadly the same regulatory stage,&quot; all undergoing security assessments required before they can seek spectrum, the radio frequencies for satellite signals.</p><p>Starlink has pursued entry into India for over five years, a market boasting more than a billion internet subscribers. Despite securing key regulatory approvals and forming partnerships with Reliance Jio and Bharti Airtel last year, the company has yet to commence commercial services. SpaceX has established a local team, appointing former Payoneer executive Prabhakar Jayakumar to lead its India operations in December. Lauren Dreyer, Starlink's Vice President of Business Operations, affirmed the company's commitment at the India Mobile Congress in New Delhi, stating, &quot;We stand ready to serve India&quot; and support Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s goal of universal connectivity.</p><p>Starlink has already deployed over 20 gateway sites and hundreds of antennas in India, adapting its operations to comply with the country's regulatory, security, and data-sovereignty requirements. SpaceX positions its satellite network as a complement to India's terrestrial telecom infrastructure, rather than a replacement. The company's first attempt to launch in India in 2021 resulted in refunds for preorders in early 2022 after the Indian government flagged it for &quot;booking/rendering the satellite internet service&quot; without necessary licenses. Starlink also previously disagreed with India's largest telecom operators over spectrum allocation, advocating for administrative assignment while Reliance Jio pushed for an auction. India ultimately favored Starlink's preferred administrative approach. Jio is collaborating with SES on satellite broadband, and Airtel is a significant backer of Eutelsat OneWeb, another licensed satellite operator in India. While its India launch timeline remains uncertain, Starlink Mobile, designed to connect ordinary phones to satellites, launched in neighboring Bangladesh this week.</p><p>What to watch: The completion of Starlink's security assessments and subsequent spectrum allocation in India.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Well-written summary that synthesizes the tech policy context, the dispute over spectrum allocation, and the current status of Starlink's regulatory hurdles.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/07/india-rejects-elon-musks-claim-of-discrimination-over-starlink-launch/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
