     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Malkajgiri Police Bust Property Fraud Network</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Malkajgiri police have arrested two individuals, Mohd. Khaja Pasha and Mohammed Zulfikhar Ali, for operating a fraud network targeting disputed and abandoned properties. A third suspect remains at large. Authorities seized forged documents, 22 fake stamps, and nine knives during raids on the suspects' residences.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/malkajgiri-police-bust-property-fraud-network.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The racket functioned by identifying vulnerable properties and impersonating original owners or legal heirs. The group used fabricated revenue stamps, fake Aadhaar cards, and counterfeit sale papers to facilitate their scheme. Police Commissioner B. Sumathi confirmed that the investigation uncovered a sophisticated operation involving computer-generated forgeries and stolen identities to illegally claim land ownership.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report concisely summarizes the arrests, the seized evidence, and the modus operandi of the fraud network as described.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/disputed-abandoned-properties-targeted-using-forged-documents-two-held-in-malkajgiri/article71556096.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
