  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/sports">sports</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-08 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sporting Club Delhi Prepares for MG ISL Opener Against Bengaluru FC</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#ISL</span> <span>#Sporting Club Delhi</span> <span>#Bengaluru FC</span> <span>#Football</span></div>
       <p>Sporting Club Delhi is set to commence its MG Indian Super League 2026-27 campaign against Bengaluru FC at the Sree Kanteerava Stadium on October 10. The Delhi-based club outlined its ambitions and approach during a pre-match press conference, attended by CEO Dhruv Sood, Head Coach Tomasz Tchorz, and midfielder Lalrinliana Hnamte, as reported by NDTV Sports.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/sporting-club-delhi-prepares-for-mg-isl-opener-against-benga.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Dhruv Sood, CEO of Sporting Club Delhi, emphasized the significance of the upcoming match, stating, &quot;The first game of a new season is always an important moment, and we are excited to begin against a club of Bengaluru's stature.&quot; He added that the club's ambition extends beyond mere participation, aiming &quot;to build a club that Delhi can connect with and be proud of.&quot; Coach Tomasz Tchorz acknowledged Bengaluru FC as a &quot;well-organised and well-structured club,&quot; making them a &quot;good benchmark&quot; for his team. He asserted, &quot;Bengaluru is a big opponent, but we are not going there with any fear. We are going there to compete and get a result,&quot; adding that &quot;nobody is unbeatable in the MG ISL.&quot;</p><p>Midfielder Lalrinliana Hnamte expressed his readiness for the season, noting, &quot;I'm mentally and physically ready for the season. We are a young team, but we are hungry for the trophy, and we believe we can have a great season.&quot; Sporting Club Delhi has strengthened its squad with a mix of experienced Indian players, emerging talent, and international recruits, with Tchorz having guided the group through an intensive pre-season. The club aims to build on foundations laid last season and establish a strong football identity representing the capital.</p><p>The match is scheduled for October 10, 2026, at 5:00 PM IST at the Sree Kanteerava Stadium in Bengaluru. Tickets are available on BookMyShow. Sporting Club Delhi, a Delhi-based football club in the Indian Super League, focuses on establishing a distinctive football identity, building a competitive team, and fostering player development and community engagement in the capital.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reports the press conference details, the match context, and the quotes from team representatives.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/football/sporting-club-delhi-set-for-mg-isl-2026-27-opener-against-bengaluru-fc-12158548#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/bengaluru/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bengaluru</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
