     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-08 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Veteran Actor Nana Patekar Dies at 75</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Veteran actor Nana Patekar has died at his Goa residence at age 75. Known for his powerful screen presence in Hindi and Marathi cinema, Patekar was a three-time National Film Award recipient and a Padma Shri honoree. His notable filmography includes works like &quot;Parinda,&quot; &quot;Krantiveer,&quot; and &quot;Khamoshi: The Musical.&quot;</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-08/veteran-actor-nana-patekar-dies-at-75.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Leaders and the film fraternity are mourning his passing, with figures like Arvind Kejriwal and Nitin Gadkari praising his artistry and social contributions. Beyond acting, Patekar was recognized for his significant work in rural Maharashtra through the Naam Foundation, focusing on water conservation and supporting families of farmers affected by suicide.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report effectively summarizes the actor's career, his social work, and the tributes paid following his passing.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
